## Field Reference

| Field | Type | Required | Description |
|-------|------|----------|-------------|
| `id` | string | Yes | Unique identifier, format: `ASSUME-NNN` |
| `type` | enum | Yes | `CONVENTION`, `BEHAVIORAL`, `INVARIANT`, `DELEGATION`, `ARCHITECTURAL`, `DOMAIN` |
| `statement` | string | Yes | The assumption in plain language |
| `source_evidence` | string | Yes | Where this assumption came from |
| `confidence` | number | Yes | 0.0–1.0, model's internal probability |
| `testable` | boolean | Yes | Can be verified automatically |
| `layer` | enum | Yes | `L1`, `L2`, `L3`, `L4` |
| `scope` | enum | Yes | `workspace`, `universal` |
| `falsifier` | string | Yes | How to prove this wrong |
| `epistemic_status` | enum | Yes | `ASSUMED_FACT`, `UNVERIFIED_PATTERN` |

## Assumption Type Guide

| Type | Template | Example |
|------|----------|---------|
| CONVENTION | "All X follow pattern Y" | "All tests use `test_*.py` naming" |
| BEHAVIORAL | "Function X does Y when Z" | "`auth.login()` returns JWT on success" |
| INVARIANT | "Condition X never occurs" | "No raw SQL in domain layer" |
| DELEGATION | "Library X handles Y" | "pytest-asyncio handles async tests" |
| ARCHITECTURAL | "System follows pattern X" | "Microservices with async messaging" |
| DOMAIN | "Domain rule X applies" | "All orders require payment confirmation" |